.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH mdmc-compile 1  "compile " 
.SH NAME
mdmc\-compile \- Compile a draft to a message (RFC 5322)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmdmc compile\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-stdout\fR] [\fB\-\-folder\fR] [\fB\-\-again\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIDRAFT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compile a draft to a message (RFC 5322)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config.toml (default ~/.config/mdmc/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-stdout\fR
Print the compiled message to stdout instead of a maildir
.TP
\fB\-\-folder\fR \fI<FOLDER>\fR
Write to this maildir: a [folders] config name or a literal path
.TP
\fB\-\-again\fR
Allow compiling a draft already marked sent
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIDRAFT\fR>
Draft filename (slug) or path to compile
